### ============================================
### PUT vs PATCH - Item Updates
### ============================================

### 1. GET existing item
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/items/foo

###

### 2. PUT - Full replacement of item
### Replaces the existing "bar" item completely.
PUT http://127.0.0.1:8000/items/bar
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Barz",
  "description": null,
  "price": 3
}

###

### 3. PATCH - Partial update of item
### Only price is changed; other existing fields are preserved.
PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/items/bar
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 25.99
}

###

### ============================================
### Error Cases
### ============================================

### 4. GET - Non-existent item (expect 404)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/items/nonexistent

###

### 5. PUT - Non-existent item (expect 404)
PUT http://127.0.0.1:8000/items/nonexistent
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test",
  "price": 10
}

###

### 6. PATCH - Non-existent item (expect 404)
PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/items/nonexistent
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 25.99
}